+- **Memory Complexity:** $O(1)$ additional memory for precomputed weights (5 vectors of size 4, 20 vectors of size 8). The main memory cost is the AMR data structure itself [S1].
+- **Measured Performance:** In the ExaJet dataset (656M cells), the builder constructed the octree representation in 160s, indicating that the GTI weight computation (precomputed) is not a bottleneck relative to file I/O [S1]. Isosurface raycasting achieves 14.28 FPS on this dataset [S1].
 - **Strengths:** Ensures $C^0$ continuity across level boundaries; avoids artifacts and cracks; adapts to AMR mesh resolution; enables artifact-free visualization [S1].
 - **Limitations:** Requires precomputation of weights for all 20 3D cases; assumes 2:1 refinement ratio; more complex to implement than standard trilinear interpolation.
